# Rust Standards

- Prefer `Result<T, E>` over panics for recoverable errors
{{#if parameters.useThiserror}}
- Use `thiserror` for library error types with `#[derive(Error)]`
{{/if}}
- Use `?` operator for error propagation
- Avoid `unwrap()` in production code paths
{{#if parameters.clippyStrict}}
- Run `cargo clippy` and fix all warnings before committing
{{/if}}
- Document public APIs with `///` doc comments
